      en: "Mũi Né Sand Dunes is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Vietnam. A unique coastal area famous for its expansive red and white sand dunes, creating a desert-like landscape. Two types of dunes: Red Dunes and White Dunes. The White Dunes are the larger and more impressive. Popular for sand-sledding and ATV rides. This landform shapes the topography of Vietnam, between the Annamite Range, karst mountains, and river deltas. Like many notable places in Vietnam, it combines regional character with the legacy of a millennia-old civilization and the French colonial era. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Vietnam — from the Mekong Delta and Ha Long Bay to the terraced rice fields."
